./docs/research/1888-wg-timers/agy-plan-r3.md:92:*   **Vulnerability:** If T8 (persistent keepalive) or T6 (passive keepalive) is due but the peer has no configured or learned endpoint, the control loop skips the keepalive send. Because no packet is sent, the activity stamp (`last_send_any_ns`) is not updated. On the next iteration, the timer will evaluate as due again. Since `timer_pass` computes the next deadline based on the stale stamps, the deadline remains in the past, causing a `timeout = 0` and a 100% CPU busy-spin.
./docs/research/1888-wg-timers/agy-plan-r3.md:114:*Justification:* The plan successfully resolves all previous findings and correctly incorporates the clock reversal to guarantee forward secrecy. However, it introduces a major busy-spin risk if keepalives are skipped on peers without resolved endpoints, along with a false-positive handshake success condition upon session expiry.
