./_Log.md:3497:  - **Action**: Issue #473 — Fix XSK bindings BPF map going stale after peer crash+reconnect. Added `verifyBindingsMapLocked()` watchdog to the 1s status poll loop. After `applyHelperStatusLocked` runs, the watchdog reads each BPF `userspace_bindings` entry and compares it against the helper's reported binding state. If a queue is Registered+Armed in the helper but the BPF map entry is all zeros, the watchdog rewrites the entry. Also repairs aliased bindings (VLAN children). This prevents silent transit traffic drops when a Compile() or HA transition zeroes the bindings map without repopulating it.
