./docs/issues/issue-history.md:12989:3. **Slow-timer decay:** halve all sketch counts on a 500 ms tick. Bounds memory usage (sketch can't grow indefinitely) and lets a recovered flow re-accumulate fair share after its burst subsides.
./docs/issues/issue-history.md:12995:Count-Min is probabilistic — collisions over-count an innocent flow when an innocent flow happens to hash into the same bucket as a misbehaving flow. Bound: false-positive rate ≤ `e / width = 2.7 / 4096 ≈ 0.07%`. Acceptable, but flag in the PR.
./docs/issues/issue-history.md:13033:Full investigation plan (after 5 review rounds + both reviewers PLAN-READY YES): `docs/line-rate-investigation-plan.md`.
./docs/issues/issue-history.md:13737:To collapse the per-flow tiers we need cross-binding per-flow accounting so that flows-on-less-busy-bindings don't consume unfair shares. The minimal version: per-flow byte-count atomic array on the lease + ECN marking (not drop) proportional to excess.
./docs/issues/issue-history.md:13896:#836 proposed promoting \`flow_bucket_head_finish_bytes\` + \`flow_bucket_tail_finish_bytes\` from per-binding to per-lease shared atomic arrays, while keeping \`queue_vtime\` per-binding. Codex hostile plan review R1 returned PLAN-READY NO with 7 HIGH + 4 MED architectural issues that cannot be closed without substantially expanding the scope. Full review at \`docs/pr/836-shared-flow-vtime/codex-plan-review.md\`.
./docs/issues/issue-history.md:13992:#835 (closed) implemented the full RSS++ rebalance loop with `ethtool -S <iface>` per-RX-ring packet counters as the load signal. 10 plan-review rounds + 3 code-review rounds settled the design (Codex PLAN-READY YES at R10, MERGE YES at R3). All 33+ unit tests passed.
