./docs/issues/issue-history.md:15217:But \`active_ns\` is 0.0004% — essentially zero. The \`thread_cpu - active - idle_spin\` = 84.47s of CPU gets attributed to IdleBlock_ns. That's the **CPU-busy ring-poll time in the idle branch** being credited to IdleBlock.
./docs/issues/issue-history.md:15228:1. delta includes: (60µs sleep time) + (~50-100 µs CPU-busy ring check & attribution & state-set from PREVIOUS idle iter) → attributed to IdleBlock (state was IdleBlock from prev iter)
./docs/issues/issue-history.md:15232:So **the CPU-busy ring-check work of each idle iteration gets attributed to IdleBlock** rather than a separate "idle-poll-cpu" bucket. That's why \`idle_block_ns\` ≫ actual sleep time.
