docs/research/1888-wg-timers/codex-plan-r2.md:25:Evidence: Linux sends a keepalive immediately after processing a handshake response when no queued data exists (`receive.c:176-186`). xpf responder sessions are unconfirmed until inbound transport (`session.rs:82-93`), and `try_encap` rejects unconfirmed current sessions as `NoSession` (`engine.rs:728-743`). v3 resets T8 on the inbound msg2 (`plan.md:152-154`) but does not send immediate transport, so a persistent-no-session handshake can leave the responder unconfirmed until the next keepalive interval.
