 succeeded in 0ms:
     1	# #1928 — virtio multi-queue forwarding outage: PLAN-READY
     2	
     3	**Status:** PLAN-READY. Root cause CONFIRMED on the venue and fixed in the Go
     4	control plane (a `clusterHA` guard on the startup HA-state publish, plus a
     5	cluster→standalone clear). The bind-flag hypothesis from earlier rounds was a
     6	MISATTRIBUTION (refuted by an isolation experiment — see below). The actual
     7	and sole root cause is a standalone HA-gate bug in the Go control plane.
     8	
     9	## Confirmed root cause (the real bug)
    10	
    11	On a **standalone** (non-chassis-cluster) firewall, the userspace dataplane
    12	dropped **all transit traffic** with disposition `HAInactive`, both IPv4 and
    13	IPv6. The chain:
    14	
    15	1. `rg_active` is a `BPF_MAP_TYPE_ARRAY` with `max_entries = 16`, so the kernel
    16	   ALWAYS exposes all 16 keys (0-15). On standalone every value is 0 (inactive).
    17	2. At snapshot-apply (`pkg/dataplane/userspace/manager.go`, the `Apply` path),
    18	   `refreshHAStateFromMapsLocked()` → `mergeHAStateFromMaps()` iterated that
    19	   array and fabricated **16 inactive HA groups** into `m.haGroups`, regardless
    20	   of cluster config (`seedHAGroupInventoryLocked` correctly no-ops without a
    21	   cluster, but the map-replay path did not).
    22	3. `syncHAStateLocked()` then shipped those 16 groups to the Rust helper
    23	   (`CTRL_REQ: update_ha_state groups=16 forwarding_armed=false` in journald).
    24	4. In the helper, `enforce_ha_resolution_snapshot()`
    25	   (`userspace-dp/src/afxdp/forwarding/mod.rs`) gates every transit
    26	   `ForwardCandidate`: with `owner_rg_id <= 0` (standalone egress ifaces have
    27	   redundancy_group 0) AND `!ha_state.is_empty()` (the 16 phantom groups), it
    28	   rewrites the disposition to `HAInactive` and drops the packet.
    29	
    30	The periodic status poll (`process.go`) already guarded the same
    31	`refreshHAStateFromMapsLocked()` behind `if m.clusterHA`. The **startup
    32	snapshot-apply path did not** — that asymmetry is the bug.
    33	
    34	## Why earlier rounds misdiagnosed it as a bind-flag issue
    35	
    36	The prior session changed `bind_flag_candidates_for_driver` (virtio AUTO →
    37	explicit COPY|NEED_WAKEUP) and observed "v6 6/6". That v6 success was **kernel
    38	return-route forwarding**, not the dataplane (`tx_completions_total` stayed 0).
    39	The "AUTO forwards nothing" observation was the HA gate dropping everything, not
    40	the bind flag. Isolation experiment on the venue (this round): with the
    41	bind-flag change REVERTED to the original `AUTO_BIND_FLAGS=[0]` (verified
    42	`flags=0x0000` in journald) but the HA-gate fix in place, the dataplane forwards
    43	**5000 pps, fwd=5000, snat=1, ha_inact=0**. So the bind-flag change was
    44	unnecessary and was DROPPED — the fix is the Go guard alone.
    45	
    46	(Diagnostic note: virtio copy-mode XSK RX delivery is fine under both AUTO and
    47	explicit-COPY binds on this kernel — `rx_xdp_redirects` climbs, the fill ring is
    48	serviced via `maybe_wake_rx`'s `poll(POLLIN)`, and `RAW: rxP`/`frC` advance with
    49	traffic. The earlier "frames never reach userspace" framing conflated the
    50	post-RX HAInactive drop with an RX-delivery failure.)
    51	
    52	## Fix
    53	
    54	`pkg/dataplane/userspace/manager.go`: guard the startup
    55	`refreshHAStateFromMapsLocked()` + `syncHAStateLocked()` behind `if m.clusterHA`,
    56	matching the pre-existing guard on the periodic status poll. When `!clusterHA`,
    57	no phantom groups are fabricated.
    58	
    59	To also cover the cluster→standalone live-reconfig hazard (Codex review Q3:
    60	stale groups a prior clustered apply pushed to the helper would otherwise keep
    61	the gate armed):
    62	- `seedHAGroupInventoryLocked` now CLEARS `m.haGroups` when there is no cluster
    63	  config (was an early return that left stale groups in the manager).
    64	- The non-cluster branch of the startup path calls a new
    65	  `clearHelperHAStateLocked()` that sends an explicit empty `update_ha_state`
    66	  (`groups=0`) so the helper rebuilds an EMPTY `ha_state` and drops any stale
    67	  groups. Verified live: the debug-log helper logged
    68	  `CTRL_REQ: update_ha_state groups=0` on a standalone apply.
    69	- The XSK-startup deferral path (manager.go, `pendingXSKStartup` early return)
    70	  also calls `clearHelperHAStateLocked()` on the non-cluster branch, because the
    71	  deferred-publish resume path (`syncSnapshotLocked`) never syncs HA state
    72	  (Codex review Q1).
    73	
    74	Regression tests:
    75	- `TestMergeHAStateFromMapsFabricatesGroupsFromArrayMap` documents the array-map
    76	  phantom-group mechanism the guard protects against.
    77	- `TestSeedHAGroupInventoryLockedClearsGroupsWithoutCluster` covers the
    78	  cluster→standalone group-clear.
    79	- `TestClearHelperHAStateLockedSendsEmptyUpdate` asserts the helper-side clear
    80	  sends `update_ha_state` with a present `ha_state` payload and 0 groups
    81	  (Codex review Q6).
    82	
    83	## Validation (venue t1921-fw, 4-queue virtio, clean production build)
    84	
    85	- v4 transit LAN→WAN: 5/5, 0% loss.
    86	- v6 transit LAN→WAN: 5/5, 0% loss.
    87	- standalone daemon: the only `update_ha_state` is the `groups=0` clear (was
    88	  `groups=16` of inactive phantom groups arming the gate).
    89	- `ha_inact=0` (was 1346 under load), `sessions` nonzero, `bpf_entries` nonzero.
    90	- `xpf_userspace_binding_tx_completions_total` nonzero across LAN+WAN bindings.
    91	- SNAT proven: wan-host has NO v4 return route to 10.66.1.0/24 yet v4 replies
    92	  returned — only possible via interface SNAT to 10.66.2.1. DBG `NAT:snat=1`.
    93	- Sustained UDP flood: `rx≈tx≈fwd=5000` per second, 0 ha_inact, 0 tx_err.
    94	
    95	## mlx5 no-regression rationale
    96	
    97	The fix only changes behavior for `clusterHA == false` (standalone). The loss
    98	cluster runs `clusterHA == true`, so the guarded block executes exactly as
    99	before — the fix is a no-op for clustered nodes. `make test-failover` confirms.
   100	
   101	## Scope
   102	
   103	- One Go guard + one regression test. No Rust helper / shim changes.
   104	- bind.rs is restored to master (the earlier #1928 bind-flag commit is dropped).

