docs/issues/issue-history.md:21931:The eBPF dataplane emits per-event records into a ring buffer at policy-deny, screen-drop, and filter-log decision points. `pkg/logging/ringbuf.go` consumes the ring buffer and produces `RT_FLOW_SESSION_DENY`, screen-drop, and filter-log syslog messages in vSRX-compatible format. The userspace dataplane's event stream (`userspace-dp/src/event_stream/`) emits ONLY SessionOpen/Close/Update. Once eBPF is removed, syslog will lose per-flow deny / screen-drop / filter-log telemetry — operators rely on these for IDS visibility and audit.
