     5	**Related issues:** Zero-copy fill ring starvation, IPv6 forwarding broken on VLAN interfaces, 40s restart gap
     6	
     7	## Problem Statement
     8	
     9	After daemon restart on the userspace HA cluster (`loss:xpf-userspace-fw0/fw1`), three problems existed:
    10	
    11	1. **IPv4 forwarding dead for 40+ seconds** after restart, even though VRRP election should provide failover in ~1s
    12	2. **IPv6 forwarding completely broken** on VLAN sub-interfaces (`ge-0-0-2.50`, `ge-0-0-2.80`) — `iperf3 -c 2001:559:8585:80::200` returned "No route to host"
    13	3. **Kernel ARP/NDP tables empty** because the XDP shim captured all ARP replies and NDP NAs, preventing the kernel from learning neighbors
    14	
    15	## Root Causes
    16	
    17	### 1. Historical XDP Shim Tail-Call Silent Failure
    18	
    19	At the time of this investigation, the Rust eBPF XDP shim
    20	(`userspace-xdp/src/lib.rs`) used `USERSPACE_FALLBACK_PROGS.tail_call()` to
    21	jump back to `xdp_main_prog` when the userspace dataplane could not handle a
    22	packet. **This tail call always silently failed** in aya-ebpf, despite the prog
    23	array being correctly populated (verified via `bpftool map dump`).
    24	
    25	Issue #1473 removed this runtime dependency: the retained userspace shim now
    26	passes only proven local/control traffic to the kernel when helper/XSK state is
    27	degraded. Non-local transit drops in both compat and strict modes and is counted
    28	as `transit_drop` in `degraded_path_counters`. The pinned BPF map still uses the
    29	internal compatibility name `userspace_fallback_stats` during mixed-version
    30	upgrades.
    31	
    32	When the tail call failed, the function fell through to `return Ok(xdp_action::XDP_DROP)`, silently dropping all fallback packets. This affected three code paths:
    33	
    34	| Path | Trigger | Old Behavior | New Behavior |
    35	|------|---------|-------------|-------------|
    36	| Historical tail-call fallback | Heartbeat missing/stale, early filter | `XDP_DROP` | Local/control pass; transit `XDP_DROP` |
    37	| Binding not ready | VLAN sub-interface without XSK binding | `XDP_DROP` | Local/control pass; transit `XDP_DROP` |
    38	| Heartbeat stale | Timeout exceeded | `XDP_DROP` | Local/control pass; transit `XDP_DROP` |
    39	
    40	**Impact:** Every packet that should have fallen back to the eBPF pipeline was silently dropped. During startup bootstrap, this meant zero forwarding.
    41	
    42	### 2. Generic XDP on VLAN Sub-Interfaces Breaks NDP
    43	
    44	The compiler attaches XDP programs to VLAN sub-interfaces (`ge-0-0-2.50`, `ge-0-0-2.80`) in `xdpgeneric` mode. When the userspace shim was swapped in, these VLAN sub-interfaces also got the shim.
